  "content": {
    "title": "Who missed cut at 2026 Masters? Bryson DeChambeau, J.J. Spaun among big names out",
    "text": "April 10, 2026, 8:34 p.m. ETSome big names will miss the weekend at Augusta National, following cuts at the 2026 Masters Tournament.The cut line following the second round was +4, leaving 37 golfers on the outside looking in for weekend play. That list includes a number of former Masters champions, including Danny Willett (2016 champion), Bubba Watson (2012, 2014), Zach Johnson (2007), Mike Weir (2003), Vijay Singh (2000), José María Olazábal (1999) and Fred Couples (1992).The list of cut players also includes last week’s winner, J.J. Spaun, who claimed the Valero Texas Open title, as well as Bryson DeChambeau, the LIV Golf star and two-time U.S. Open champion.Reigning Masters champion Rory McIlroy has dominated through two rounds and will take a 6-shot lead into the third round over Patrick Reed and Sam Burns, who are tied for second.Here are the golfers who missed the cut at the 2026 Masters:Danny Willett — +5Harry Hall — +5J.J. Spaun — +5Ryan Fox — +5Bubba Watson — +5Zach Johnson — +6Nicolai Højgaard — +6Akshay Bhatia — +6Bryson DeChambeau — +6Andrew Novak — +7Tom McKibbin — +7Robert MacIntyre — +7Rasmus Neergaard-Petersen — +7Cameron Smith — +7Michael Kim — +8Ethan Fang (a) — +8Daniel Berger — +8Jackson Herrington (a) — +8Casey Jarvis — +8Fred Couples — +9José María Olazábal — +9Mason Howell (a) — +9Mike Weir — +10Vijay Singh — +10Min Woo Lee — +11Fifa Laopakdee (a) — +11Johnny Keefer — +11Carlos Ortiz — +11Sami Valimaki — +11Max Greyserman — +12Nico Echavarria — +13Mateo Pulcini (a) — +15Naoyuki Kataoka — +15Aldrich Potgieter — +15Brandon Holtz (a) — +15Ángel Cabrera — +16Davis Riley — +18",
